          "lexical_rank": 1,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: When is payment due, and what payment methods do you accept?\nAnswer: Payment is due at the time of service. We accept cash, major credit and debit cards (Visa, Mastercard, American Express), and Flexible Spending Account (FSA) / Health Savings Account (HSA) cards.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 35,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.33439642,
          "dense_rank": 2,
          "lexical_score": 2.6380072,
          "lexical_rank": 16,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## The self-check-in kiosk\n\nReturning patients can check in at the kiosk beside the front desk instead of queuing. Scan the QR code from your 48-hour reminder text, or type in your last name and date of birth. The kiosk cannot take payments: any copay or self-pay amount is paid at the front desk.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 24,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.32418,
          "dense_rank": 3,
          "lexical_score": 2.7888374,
          "lexical_rank": 13,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I do if my insurance isn't listed or I am out-of-network?\nAnswer: You can pay out-of-pocket for your visit, and we can provide you with an itemized receipt to submit to your insurer for potential reimbursement.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 29,
          "chunk_index": 6,
          "similarity_score": 0.30605316,
          "dense_rank": 4,
          "lexical_score": 3.109383,
          "lexical_rank": 6,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Copays and deductibles\n\nYour plan decides how much you pay at the visit. A copay is a fixed amount your plan sets for each visit, and it is collected when you check in. If your plan has a deductible you have not met yet, you pay the amount your plan allows for the visit at check-in. The front desk can estimate that amount for you if you give them your plan details before the visit.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 29,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.30126038,
          "dense_rank": 5,
          "lexical_score": 3.0043566,
          "lexical_rank": 11,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Blue Cross Blue Shield\n\nWe are in-network with Blue Cross Blue Shield PPO plans, including BlueCard PPO members whose plan was issued in another state; look for the suitcase logo with the letters \"PPO\" on your card. The Federal Employee Program (FEP) Basic Option and Standard Option plans are in-network too. We are not in-network with Blue Essentials HMO or Blue Advantage HMO plans, because those plans only cover care from their own medical groups.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 34,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.30076778,
          "dense_rank": 6,
          "lexical_score": 3.1305344,
          "lexical_rank": 5,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Appointment reminders and messages from the clinic\n## Messages we will never send\n\nWe will never ask for your card number, bank details, Social Security number or insurance member ID by text message",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 38,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.2910437,
          "dense_rank": 7,
          "lexical_score": 2.7961044,
          "lexical_rank": 12,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n## A code you do not recognise\n\nIf your receipt shows a code that is not in this list, the front desk can tell you what it is.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 23,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.28495148,
          "dense_rank": 8,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Which health insurance plans do you accept?\nAnswer: We accept most major insurance providers, including Blue Cross Blue Shield, Aetna, Cigna, UnitedHealthcare, and Medicare. If you're unsure",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 29,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.28475228,
          "dense_rank": 9,
          "lexical_score": 3.0848086,
          "lexical_rank": 8,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n\nThis guide lists, plan by plan, the health insurance plans we are in-network with. Insurance companies sell many plans under one brand name, and being in-network with a company",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 38,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.27521348,
          "dense_rank": 10,
          "lexical_score": 3.1048849,
          "lexical_rank": 7,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n\nYour itemized receipt lists each procedure done at your visit by its billing code. Medical procedures use five-digit CPT codes, and dental procedures use CDT cod",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
